    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.40) standing as our premier offensive anchor. His favorable platoon matchup against the left-handed Suarez, combined with a significant park factor boost, positions him to lead our production. He is closely followed by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (71.84) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.27), both of whom benefit from positive SP skill metrics and high-leverage lineup slots. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a tougher matchup against Suarez, his elite park factor keeps his efficiency firmly in our starting rotation, ensuring we maintain high-ceiling potential across the middle of our order.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Liam Hicks**, who fell just shy of the starting threshold with a score of 39.70. While his platoon advantage against Williams was promising, the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile ultimately suppressed his output below our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor. Elsewhere, we are leaning heavily into the speed profiles of **Sam Antonacci** (61.10) and **Nasim Nunez** (41.04); while **Nasim Nunez** carries a lower score due to his position at the bottom of the order, his utility in stealing bases\u2014our scarcest category\u2014keeps him active despite the SP matchup against Snell. \n\nWe are monitoring the **Drake Baldwin** situation closely, as he faces a challenging 2.81 xERA arm in S\u00e1nchez. His score is buoyed primarily by elite BvP data and an advantageous spot in the two-hole, but he represents a higher-risk play today. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (45.39) faces a difficult assignment against Fried, and while he remains in the lineup, we will be watching his early-game performance closely given the lack of platoon support and the presence of a pitcher capable of suppressing base-path aggression. We remain without **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Heliot Ramos**, all of whom are currently unavailable due to injury or benching, forcing us to lean on the depth of our bench assets like **Andy Pages**, **Ryan Clifford**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Lara**, **Tommy White**, **Franklin Arias**, and **Henry Bolte** if mid-game pinch-hit situations arise.",
